# Masking Scanner Rules

- The scanner must preserve character lengths and newlines exactly (`masked.length === text.length`).
- Comments, strings, and regex literals are blanked to space characters.
- Non-code spans are classified into `{ kind: "comment" | "string" | "regex", start, end }`.
- Nested template interpolations `${...}` are handled to arbitrary depth.
- Adversarial tests in `test/tokenize.test.mjs` must accompany any scanner modifications.
